/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"Max concurrent trials for one case."},"2134":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-54","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"`pass_threshold`"},"2135":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-55","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"float"},"2136":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-56","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"no"},"2137":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-57","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"`1.0`"},"2138":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-58","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"Fraction of trials that must pass for a case to be marked passed; validated to `[0.0, 1.0]` (`EVAL_INVALID_THRESHOLD` otherwise)."},"2139":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-59","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"`fail_on_missing_agent`"},"2140":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-60","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"bool"},"2141":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-61","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"no"},"2142":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-62","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"**`true`**"},"2143":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-63","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"If true, `eval run` and `eval validate --agent <key>` error with `EVAL_AGENT_UNAVAILABLE` when the chosen agent isn't installed."},"2144":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-64","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"**Defaults verified against source** (`crates/fastskill-core/src/core/manifest.rs::EvalConfigToml`): `timeout_seconds` defaults to **900**, and `fail_on_missing_agent` defaults to **true** — the CLI refuses to run against a missing agent unless you explicitly set it to `false`. Don't assume otherwise from older examples."},"2145":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-65","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"With no `checks` file configured, each case still receives the required skill-consultation expectation implied by `should_trigger`. A successful process exit alone is not enough. Add a checks file for further deterministic outcome or adherence evidence."},"2146":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-66","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#validate-the-config","content":"Real output against a working config (this one set `timeout_seconds = 120` and `fail_on_missing_agent = false`):"},"2147":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-67","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#validate-the-config","content":"(`parallel: 0` here just means \"unset\" in the table renderer — the runner still falls back to CPU core count.) A broken `checks.toml` fails validation immediately, e.g.:"},"2148":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-68","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#validate-the-config","content":"A prompts CSV missing a required column fails the same way:"},"2149":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-69","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"The suite loader (`aikit-evals::suite`) reads a header row with **required** columns `id`, `prompt`, `should_trigger`, plus optional `tags` and `workspace_subdir`."},"2150":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-70","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"Column"},"2151":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-71","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"Required"},"2152":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-72","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"Meaning"},"2153":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-73","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"`id`"},"2154":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-74","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"yes"},"2155":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-75","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"Non-empty identifier per row. Used for `--case`, artifact folder names, and reports."},"2156":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-76","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"`prompt`"},"2157":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-77","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"yes"},"2158":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-78","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"Text sent to the agent. Use CSV quoting (`\"...\"`, doubled `\"\"` for an embedded quote) for commas or newlines."},"2159":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-79","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"`should_trigger`"},"2160":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-80","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"yes"},"2161":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-81","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"`true`/`1` (case-insensitive `true`) or anything else counts as `false`. It creates a required per-case skill-consultation expectation; see below."},"2162":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-82","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"`tags`"},"2163":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-83","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"no"},"2164":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-84","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"Comma-separated tags inside the cell (e.g. `\"smoke,basic\"`). Used by `eval run --tag <name>`."},"2165":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-85","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"`workspace_subdir`"},"2166":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-86","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"no"},"2167":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-87","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"Relative path that becomes the agent's working directory for the case. Under the default isolation it is created **inside the case's scratch workspace**, with fixture files copied in from the same path under the project root; under `--no-isolation` it resolves directly under the project root. Empty or omitted → workspace root."},"2168":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-88","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"Empty lines are skipped."},"2169":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-89","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"**`should_trigger` affects pass/fail.** The engine creates an implicit required `skill_invoked` check for each case, with `expected` equal to the CSV value. An explicit `skill_invoked` check that applies to the case replaces the implicit one; `eval validate` rejects a contradictory polarity. Therefore `false` tests non-consultation and `true` tests consultation, subject to the selected backend's observability."},"2170":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-90","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"This is adherence/selection evidence, not outcome correctness. A structured `Skill` call is direct evidence; supported decoders may also recognize a tool input that references the staged skill-document path. The path proxy indicates consultation, not that the instructions were read or followed. Pair positive cases with outcome checks or judges."},"2171":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-91","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#3-checks-checkstoml-optional","content":"Point `checks` at a TOML file with one or more `[[check]]` tables, keyed by the required `name` field. There are exactly five check types (`aikit_evals::checks::CheckDefinition`):"},"2172":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-92","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#3-checks-checkstoml-optional","content":"**Checks score the canonical trace, never raw stdout.** Every check below matches against the run's `trace.jsonl` — the parsed, structured event stream. Raw stdout is deliberately excluded: with the `claude` agent it opens with a `system`/`project init` event listing **every skill installed in the environment**, which used to make any skill-name pattern pass vacuously. Assistant text still reaches the trace as message events, so matching on what the agent actually said continues to work."},"2173":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-93","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"The check you almost certainly want for \"did my skill fire?\"."},"2174":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-94","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"Field"},"2175":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-95","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"Type"},"2176":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-96","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"Required"},"2177":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-97","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"Default"},"2178":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-98","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"`skill`"},"2179":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-99","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"string"},"2180":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-100","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"no"},"2181":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-101","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"— (omit to match *any* skill invocation)"},"2182":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-102","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"`expected`"},"2183":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-103","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"bool"},"2184":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-104","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"no"},"2185":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-105","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"`true` (`false` asserts the skill did **not** run)"},"2186":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-106","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"`required`"},"2187":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-107","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"bool"},"2188":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-108","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"no"},"2189":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-109","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"`true`"},"2190":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-110","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"`cases`"},"2191":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-111","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"string array"},"2192":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-112","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"no"},"2193":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-113","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"all cases (exact case IDs)"},"2194":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-114","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"Matches a structured `Skill` invocation or, where the decoder supplies it, a tool input referring to the staged skill-document path. When `skill` is given, a structured invocation must exactly match its identifying field. A skill name merely mentioned in unrelated prose does not count. Path-reference matching improves portability but remains a consultation proxy rather than proof of adherence."},"2195":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-115","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"Every check type supports `cases = [\"case-id\", ...]`, selecting exact case IDs. An absent selector applies to every case. Use selectors for checks that should not run across a mixed suite."},"2196":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-116","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"Field"},"2197":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-117","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"Type"},"2198":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-118","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"Required"},"2199":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-119","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"Default"},"2200":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-120","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"`pattern`"},"2201":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-121","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"string"},"2202":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-122","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"yes"},"2203":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-123","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"—"},"2204":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-124","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"`expected`"},"2205":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-125","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"bool"},"2206":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-126","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"yes"},"2207":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-127","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"— (`true` = pattern must appear, `false` = must NOT appear)"},"2208":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-128","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"`required`"},"2209":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-129","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"bool"},"2210":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-130","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"no"},"2211":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-131","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"`true`"},"2212":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-132","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"Matches `pattern` as a **plain substring** against the JSONL trace. Prefer `skill_invoked` for asserting that a skill ran; treat `trigger_expectation` as the escape hatch for matching arbitrary text the agent produced."},"2213":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-133","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"Field"},"2214":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-134","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"Type"},"2215":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-135","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"Required"},"2216":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-136","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"Default"},"2217":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-137","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"`pattern`"},"2218":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-138","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"string"},"2219":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-139","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"yes"},"2220":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-140","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"—"},"2221":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-141","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"`required`"},"2222":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-142","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"bool"},"2223":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-143","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"no"},"2224":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-144","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"`true`"},"2225":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-145","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"Same trace substring search as `trigger_expectation`, without the pass/fail inversion — passes if the pattern is found anywhere in the trace."},"2226":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-146","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"Field"},"2227":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-147","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"Type"},"2228":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-148","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"Required"},"2229":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-149","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"Default"},"2230":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-150","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"`path`"},"2231":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-151","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"path"},"2232":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-152","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"yes"},"2233":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-153","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"—"},"2234":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-154","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"`required`"},"2235":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-155","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"bool"},"2236":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-156","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"no"},"2237":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-157","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"`true`"},"2238":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-158","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"Passes if `path` exists under the case's working directory — the case's scratch workspace under the default isolation (plus `workspace_subdir` when set), or the project root under `--no-isolation`."},"2239":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-159","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"Field"},"2240":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-160","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"Type"},"2241":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-161","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"Required"},"2242":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-162","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"Default"},"2243":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-163","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"`limit`"},"2244":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-164","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"integer"},"2245":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-165","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"yes"},"2246":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-166","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"—"},"2247":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-167","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"`required`"},"2248":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-168","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"bool"},"2249":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-169","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"no"},"2250":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-170","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"`true`"},"2251":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-171","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"Passes if the number of **tool invocations** the agent made is `<= limit`."},"2252":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-172","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"A tool invocation is a structured `tool_use` trace event, plus any `raw_json` trace line — the\nlatter covers backends that still emit tool calls as raw JSON instead of decoded tool events.\nAssistant text output, token-usage events, and unmodelled SDK event variants are **not** counted."},"2253":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-173","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"Results use `\"check_name\": \"max_tool_calls\"`. The per-case artifact field counting\nthese events is `command_count`."},"2254":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-174","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#making-a-check-advisory-with-required","content":"Every check type accepts `required` (default `true`). Setting `required = false` makes the check **advisory**: it still runs, and its result still appears in the run artifacts with its own `passed` value, but a failure does not fail the case."},"2255":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-175","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#making-a-check-advisory-with-required","content":"Use it for signal you want visible in reports without gating the suite on it."},"2256":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-176","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#how-a-cases-passfail-is-decided","content":"No `checks` file configured (or it loads zero explicit checks): the case still receives the required trigger expectation generated from `should_trigger`."},"2257":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-177","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#how-a-cases-passfail-is-decided","content":"Any checks loaded: the case **passes** only if every **required** check's `passed` is `true`. Checks marked `required = false` are reported but never fail the case. Among required checks there is no partial credit and no threshold — they are all-or-nothing per case."},"2258":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-178","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#how-a-cases-passfail-is-decided","content":"A case whose checks are **all** advisory (`required = false`) has nothing that can fail it, so it passes as long as it does not time out. That is intentional, but it means an all-optional `checks.toml` is not a safety net."},"2259":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-179","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#how-a-cases-passfail-is-decided","content":"A trial that times out is always `error`, independent of checks."},"2260":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-180","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#how-a-cases-passfail-is-decided","content":"Across trials, `pass_threshold` decides the case's aggregated status: pass rate across trials must be `>= pass_threshold`."},"2261":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-181","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#4-validate-then-run-then-report","content":"Once the manifest, CSV, and checks file exist:"},"2262":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-182","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#4-validate-then-run-then-report","content":"`--output-dir` is **required** on `fastskill eval run` — there is no default. Omitting it fails argument parsing before anything else runs:"},"2263":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-183","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#4-validate-then-run-then-report","content":"`--agent <key>` (repeatable) and `--all` are mutually exclusive on both `eval run` and `eval validate` — passing both errors with `RUNTIME_CONFLICTING_FLAGS`. `eval run` additionally requires one of them (passing neither errors with `RUNTIME_NO_SELECTION`); on `eval validate` both are optional — omit them to validate config without checking any agent's availability."},"2264":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-184","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#4-validate-then-run-then-report","content":"See Run evals for the full day-to-day command set, artifact layout, and CI gating pattern."},"2265":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-185","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#setup-checklist","content":"`[tool.fastskill.eval]` present with a `prompts` path that resolves."},"2266":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-186","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#setup-checklist","content":"Prompts CSV has `id`, `prompt`, `should_trigger` headers (plus `tags` / `workspace_subdir` if you use them)."},"2267":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-187","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#setup-checklist","content":"Each `should_trigger` value reflects the required consultation/non-consultation expectation; explicit `skill_invoked` checks do not contradict it."},"2268":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-188","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#setup-checklist","content":"Outcome correctness is measured separately where consultation alone is insufficient."},"2269":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-189","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#setup-checklist","content":"`fastskill eval validate --all` passes and lists the agent you intend to run against as available."},"2270":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-190","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#setup-checklist","content":"Output directory convention agreed for `--output-dir` (local + CI)."},"2271":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-191","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#see-also","content":"Run evals"},"2272":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-192","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#see-also","content":"Cluster analysis"},"2273":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-193","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#see-also","content":"eval command"},"2274":{"id":"/integration/agents","page_id":"/integration/agents","type":"page","content":"Documentation and tools for agents","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Connect agents","Agent setup"],"tags":[],"url":"/integration/agents"},"2275":{"id":"/integration/agents-0","page_id":"/integration/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/agents","content":"Retrieve current FastSkill documentation as Markdown and use the CLI or MCP safely."},"2276":{"id":"/integration/agents-1","page_id":"/integration/agents","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/agents#read-the-documentation","content":"Read the documentation"},"2277":{"id":"/integration/agents-2","page_id":"/integration/agents","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/agents#inspect-the-cli-contract","content":"Inspect the CLI contract"},"2278":{"id":"/integration/agents-3","page_id":"/integration/agents","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/agents#preview-apply-verify","content":"Preview, apply, verify"},"2279":{"id":"/integration/agents-4","page_id":"/integration/agents","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/agents#agent-skills-and-mcp","content":"Agent skills and MCP"},"2280":{"id":"/integration/agents-5","page_id":"/integration/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/agents#read-the-documentation","content":"This site documents one release. The release number appears on every page and in\nall Markdown exports. Start with llms.txt, follow its per-page Markdown\nlinks, or download llms-full.txt. These URLs need no authentication\nor browser JavaScript. Each page also provides View Markdown and Copy Markdown."},"2281":{"id":"/integration/agents-6","page_id":"/integration/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/agents#inspect-the-cli-contract","content":"Match the binary version to the documentation. `cli spec` describes the installed\nbinary's complete command tree and flags. Use only the flags supported by that\ncommand; `--json` is not a global flag."},"2282":{"id":"/integration/agents-7","page_id":"/integration/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/agents#preview-apply-verify","content":"Check the process exit status and the returned diagnostics. A valid JSON response\ncan describe failure or partial success. Dry runs validate a plan without changing\nmanaged state; online plans can still fetch inputs. Use `--offline` when supported\nand when required verified content is already available locally."},"2283":{"id":"/integration/agents-8","page_id":"/integration/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/agents#agent-skills-and-mcp","content":"Installed skills provide task instructions. FastSkill's MCP tools provide package\noperations. They are separate interfaces; reading a skill does not require an MCP\nserver. See Claude Code and\nCursor for installation locations and registration."},"2284":{"id":"/integration/agents-9","page_id":"/integration/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/agents#agent-skills-and-mcp","content":"The server exposes read-only tools by default. Mutating tools require\n`mcp serve --enable-write`. Tool names use the full command path, for example\n`fastskill_skill_read` and `fastskill_project_install`. See\nMCP tool access for write configuration."},"2285":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","type":"page","content":"Claude Code Integration","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Connect agents","Agent setup"],"tags":[],"url":"/integration/claude-code-integration"},"2286":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-0","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration","content":"Integrate FastSkill with Claude Code for intelligent skill discovery."},"2287":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-1","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#overview","content":"Overview"},"2288":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-2","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#quick-start","content":"Quick start"},"2289":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-3","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#how-it-works","content":"How it works"},"2290":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-4","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#github-actions","content":"GitHub Actions"},"2291":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-5","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"2292":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-6","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#mcp-registration","content":"MCP Registration"},"2293":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-7","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#http-api","content":"HTTP API"},"2294":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-8","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#overview","content":"Claude Code reads skills **directly** from the skills directory (`.claude/skills/` by\ndefault). FastSkill's job is to get the right skills onto disk and keep them reconciled with\nyour manifest — once a skill is installed, Claude Code discovers it natively. There is no\nmetadata file to generate or keep in sync."},"2295":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-9","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#quick-start","content":"That's it — the next time Claude Code runs in this project, the installed skills are available."},"2296":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-10","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#how-it-works","content":"`fastskill project install` / `fastskill skill add` materializes skills into the configured\n`skills_directory` (default `.claude/skills/`)."},"2297":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-11","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#how-it-works","content":"Each skill is a folder containing `SKILL.md` plus its resources."},"2298":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-12","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#how-it-works","content":"Claude Code scans that directory and loads skills by their `SKILL.md` frontmatter — no\nexport or sync step is involved."},"2299":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-13","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#how-it-works","content":"Use `fastskill skill read <skill-id>` to see exactly what an agent loads, or\n`fastskill skill read <skill-id> --meta` for just the metadata."},"2300":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-14","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#github-actions","content":"Keep the skills directory reconciled in CI so commits always carry the resolved skill set:"},"2301":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-15","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#troubleshooting","content":"**Claude Code doesn't see a skill:** Confirm it is installed with `fastskill skill list`, and that\nthe skills directory contains a valid `SKILL.md` for it. `fastskill skill read <skill-id>` should\nprint its content."},"2302":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-16","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#troubleshooting","content":"**Wrong skills directory:** Claude Code and FastSkill must agree on the location. The default\nis `.claude/skills/`; override it via `skills_directory` under `[tool.fastskill]` in\n`skill-project.toml` or the `--skills-dir` flag."},"2303":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-17","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#mcp-registration","content":"Register `fastskill` as an MCP server inside Claude Code with a single command:"},"2304":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-18","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#mcp-registration","content":"After running the command, reload Claude Code. The tools exposed by\n`fastskill mcp serve --transport stdio` will be callable from the agent — the read-only ones only.\nMutating tools (`fastskill_project_install`, `fastskill_skill_add`,\n`fastskill_skill_remove`, …) require `mcp serve --enable-write`; see\nWrite access."},"2305":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-19","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#http-api","content":"`fastskill server serve` exposes FastSkill's versioned application API under `/api/v1/…`, for example `GET /api/v1/status` and `GET /api/v1/skills`."},"2306":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-20","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#http-api","content":"The old Claude-compatible `/v1/skills…` HTTP surface is no longer part of the public server. Use the MCP integration above for Claude Code and use `/api/v1/…` for HTTP clients."},"2307":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-21","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#http-api","content":"See the agent’s skill documentation for native discovery behavior."},"2308":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","type":"page","content":"Cursor Integration","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Connect agents","Agent setup"],"tags":[],"url":"/integration/cursor-integration"},"2309":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-0","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/cursor-integration","content":"Integrate FastSkill with Cursor IDE for intelligent skill discovery and tool recommendations."},"2310":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-1","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/cursor-integration#overview","content":"Overview"},"2311":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integrati