irectly** from the skills directory (`.claude/skills/` by default)\nand via the FastSkill MCP server. FastSkill's job is to install the right skills onto disk and\nkeep them reconciled with your manifest — there is no metadata file to generate or keep in sync."},"2321":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-12","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/cursor-integration#overview","content":"Modern agents (Cursor, Claude Code, …) read installed skills from the skills directory natively.\nJust `fastskill project install` (or `fastskill skill add`) and the skills are available. Register the MCP\nserver below for richer, tool-based access from inside Cursor."},"2322":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-13","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/cursor-integration#mcp-registration","content":"Register `fastskill` as an MCP server inside Cursor with a single command:"},"2323":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-14","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/cursor-integration#mcp-registration","content":"After running the command, reload Cursor. The tools exposed by\n`fastskill mcp serve --transport stdio` will be callable from the agent — the read-only ones only.\nMutating tools (`fastskill_project_install`, `fastskill_skill_add`,\n`fastskill_skill_remove`, …) require\n`mcp serve --enable-write`; see Write access."},"2324":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-15","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/cursor-integration#how-cursor-uses-the-skills","content":"When you ask Cursor to perform a task, it:"},"2325":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-16","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/cursor-integration#how-cursor-uses-the-skills","content":"**Reads available skills** from the skills directory (and the FastSkill MCP server, if\nregistered)."},"2326":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-17","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/cursor-integration#how-cursor-uses-the-skills","content":"**Matches task requirements** against each skill's `description` frontmatter."},"2327":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-18","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/cursor-integration#how-cursor-uses-the-skills","content":"**Loads the full `SKILL.md`** for relevant skills to get instructions and parameters —\nthe same content `fastskill skill read <skill-id>` prints."},"2328":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-19","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/cursor-integration#example","content":"**User query:*&#x2A; &#x2A;\"Help me create a PowerPoint presentation for my quarterly review.\"*"},"2329":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-20","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/cursor-integration#example","content":"Cursor scans installed skills for presentation-related descriptions, finds a match (e.g.\n`pptx`), loads its `SKILL.md`, and follows the skill's instructions to complete the task."},"2330":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-21","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/cursor-integration#configuration","content":"Ensure your project has a `skill-project.toml` and that Cursor and FastSkill agree on the\nskills directory. The default is `.claude/skills/`; override it via `skills_directory` under\n`[tool.fastskill]` in `skill-project.toml` or the `--skills-dir` flag."},"2331":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-22","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/cursor-integration#automation","content":"Keep the skills directory reconciled in CI so commits always carry the resolved skill set:"},"2332":{"