,"page_id":"/optimize/results","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/optimize/results#diffs-and-skill-versions","content":"Versioned skill documents live at `<run>/skills/skill_v{NNNN}.md`, not in the step\ndirectory."},"2605":{"id":"/optimize/results-35","page_id":"/optimize/results","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/optimize/results#diffs-and-skill-versions","content":"**A new version is written only when a step is accepted**, so version numbers count\n*accepted steps*, not steps. Once any step has been rejected they no longer line up with\nstep indices: if step 0 is rejected and step 1 accepted, step 1's diff is\n`skill_v0000.md → skill_v0001.md`, not `v0001 → v0002`."},"2606":{"id":"/optimize/results-36","page_id":"/optimize/results","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/optimize/results#diffs-and-skill-versions","content":"`--show diffs` therefore resolves the bracketing versions from `history.json` — counting\naccepted steps before the one you asked for — rather than assuming step N maps to version\nN. For a rejected step it reports that directly:"},"2607":{"id":"/optimize/results-37","page_id":"/optimize/results","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/optimize/results#diffs-and-skill-versions","content":"If the step isn't recorded in `history.json` at all, `inspect` says that instead of\nguessing."},"2608":{"id":"/optimize/results-38","page_id":"/optimize/results","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/optimize/results#rollouts","content":"`rollouts.json` holds the per-case scores behind the step's aggregate, surfaced under\n`--show all`:"},"2609":{"id":"/optimize/results-39","page_id":"/optimize/results","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/optimize/results#finding-a-step-to-inspect","content":"Use `status` to read the history table first, then pick the step you care about — the\nlargest positive delta, or the last accepted step before a regression:"},"2610":{"id":"/optimize/results-40","page_id":"/optimize/results","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/optimize/results#finding-a-step-to-inspect","content":"An empty table under a completed run means no training steps were recorded — see the\nzero-step warning in Running and monitoring."},"2611":{"id":"/optimize/results-41","page_id":"/optimize/results","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/optimize/results#export-the-best-skill","content":"When you're happy with the results, export the best skill document:"},"2612":{"id":"/optimize/results-42","page_id":"/optimize/results","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/optimize/results#export-the-best-skill","content":"This copies `best_skill.md` from the run directory to the destination path. Parent\ndirectories are created if they don't exist."},"2613":{"id":"/optimize/results-43","page_id":"/optimize/results","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/optimize/results#export-the-best-skill","content":"**Note:** `best_skill.md` is the highest-scoring skill document seen across all accepted\nsteps — not necessarily the final step. If the last few steps were rejected, it reflects the\nbest earlier checkpoint. A run where nothing was accepted exports the seed document, with\nthe optimizer's protected-region markers added."},"2614":{"id":"/optimize/results-44","page_id":"/optimize/results","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/optimize/results#artifacts-reference","content":"Each step directory (`<run>/steps/step_{NNNN}/`) contains:"},"2615":{"id":"/optimize/results-45","page_id":"/optimize/results","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/optimize/results#artifacts-reference","content":"File"},"2616":{"id":"/optimize/results-46","page_id":"/optimize/results","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/optimize/results#artifacts-reference","content":"Description"},"2617":{"id":"/optimize/results-47","page_id":"/optimize/results","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/optimize/results#artifacts-reference","content":"`patch.json`"},"2618":{"id":"/optimize/results-48","page_id":"/optimize/results","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/optimize/results#artifacts-reference","content":"Array of edits proposed by the optimizer (`op`, `t