;*`fastskill server serve`** exposes an HTTP API and web UI for browsing and integration."],[311,"The project manifest is `skill-project.toml`. The skill's source is separate from\nits installation directory, `.claude/skills`."],[224,"The quickstart creates a skill, installs it, verifies its contents,\nand makes it available to an agent. It needs no registry or API key."],[2592,"The raw JSON patch the optimizer proposed (`patch.json`)"],[2847,"The registry index is an on-disk NDJSON catalog read by `fastskill server serve` and the registry search endpoints. It is populated externally (for example, by the platform operator that hosts the registry) rather than by a self-hosted CLI write path."],[2848,"The registry index uses a simple org/package directory structure:"],[3038,"The registry validates `marketplace.json` files:"],[2798,"The response ranks installed skills by relevance to the prompt so the agent can pull just the top\nmatches into context. `resolve` is a **read** endpoint — it works whether or not `server serve` was started\nwith `--enable-write`."],[426,"The result is `dist/notes-team-1.0.0.zip`. Its embedded identity, version, membership, and\ndigests are authoritative, so renaming the download does not change the release."],[2688,"The run directory is safe to copy, archive, or share. Resume and inspect commands only need this directory."],[2540,"The run directory records every step's artifacts for inspection."],[637,"The runs under `--root` carry more than one `(agent, model)`"],[351,"The safest way to recover is to delete the corrupted lock and regenerate it:"],[640,"The same case id is measured by more than one run"],[2774,"The same trap applies if every check you configure is `required = false`: scoring filters to required checks, so an all-advisory file leaves nothing to score and every case reads `1.0`. Keep at least one required check."],[249,"The script picks the archive for your platform, checks it against the release's\n`SHA256SUMS`, installs `fastskill` into `~/.local/bin` (`%USERPROFILE%\\.local\\bin` on\nWindows) and adds that directory to PATH. Open a new shell, then run `fastskill -V`."],[2284,"The server exposes read-only tools by default. Mutating tools require\n`mcp serve --enable-write`. Tool names use the full command path, for example\n`fastskill_skill_read` and `fastskill_project_install`. See\nMCP tool access for write configuration."],[1512,"The server exposes two standard health endpoints immediately after startup:"],[3115,"The server has no built-in authentication. Use it locally, or put authentication\nand network restrictions in front of it when exposing it to other users. Read-only\naccess still reveals skill content. See the security model."],[3317,"The server is **read-only by default**: the mutating commands are not exported as tools unless you\nstart it with `--enable-write`. See Write access below."],[438,"The shared Manifest can declare skills from multiple Git repositories, configured repositories,\nZIP URLs, or shared paths. `project install` resolves the combined roots and the consuming project\nwrites the exact results to its own `skills.lock`. References may be nested. FastSkill rejects\nmissing files, reference cycles, and incompatible declarations of the same skill ID."],[749,"The skill ID (directory name) must meet these requirements:"],[3205,"The skills directory contains the installed files an agent reads."],[3264,"The skills directory exists and is a directory"],[3247,"The standard validator expects a lowercase name of 1–64 characters using letters,\ndigits, and single separating hyphens. The description must be nonempty and at most\n1024 characters. Name and description help an agent decide when to load the skill."],[2514,"The suite CSV has zero cases tagged `selection`. Exact message: `OPTIMIZE_NO_SELECTION_CASES: suite has zero cases tagged 'selection'`."],[2516,"The suite CSV has zero cases tagged `train` (e.g. every row is `selection`/`test`). See Setup for the exact message and the full split model."],[2705,"The suite is a CSV file with one row per eval case. Required columns:"],[2149,"The suite loader (`aikit-evals::suite`) reads a header row with **required** columns `id`, `prompt`, `should_trigger`, plus optional `tags` and `workspace_subdir`."],[545,"The summary reports what each run actually got (`isolation:` line in table output, `isolation` object in `summary.json`), and a failed case's scratch workspace is kept under `<run-dir>/workspaces/` for debugging. Pass `--no-isolation` to restore the old inherit-everything behaviour."],[2794,"The task text to resolve against. Must not be empty (`RESOLVE_EMPTY_PROMPT`)."],[2695,"The three splits"],[1025,"The tree contains 49 leaf commands. Root help shows the namespaces as a compact table of contents.\nRun `fastskill <namespace> --help` to discover that namespace, then run\n`fastskill <namespace> <action> --help` for arguments and examples. A bare skill ID is not a\ncommand; use `fastskill skill read <skill-id>`."],[3258,"The two tools for debugging FastSkill are `fastskill cli doctor` — an environment/configuration health\ncheck — and the global `--verbose` / `-v` flag for detailed command output."],[2714,"The user message sent to the target agent."],[2660,"The usual cause is a suite with no `train` rows, which `optimization run` now rejects up front\nwith `OPTIMIZE_NO_TRAIN_CASES` (see Setup). This warning is the\nbackstop for every other way a run can end up doing nothing — for example a loop\nconfiguration that yields no steps. Treat it as a failed run, not a successful one:\n`best_skill.md` is the seed document, unchanged."],[3287,"The way you test a skill in FastSkill is `fastskill eval`. You define eval cases in your project\nmanifest, run them against an agent, and score the results. There is no separate unit/mock harness —\neval is the testing framework."],[431,"Then restore the exact locked release:"],[2805,"There are no cache-size, eviction, or tuning knobs to config